This repository contains code and data under different terms. Each part keeps the terms of its authors.

1. ROMs (src/roms/)
   ----------------
   The ROM images are not covered by the MIT license below and no license to them is granted here. They are
   included, as with ZX Spectrum emulators and other FPGA cores, so that the core works out of the box, and they are
   packed into quadspeccy.kg by the build. Their rights stay with their owners:

   - 128.rom, 48.rom: the ZX Spectrum 128 / 48 ROMs, copyright (c) Amstrad plc. Amstrad allows them to be
     distributed with emulators, without charge for them.
   - esxdos089.bin: esxDOS 0.8.9 for DivMMC, Papaya Dezign (https://esxdos.org). Freeware
     with no published license ("All rights perversed", README.TXT of the esxDOS package); free to download from
     esxdos.org.
   - trdos504tprofiD.rom: TR-DOS 5.04T with the Profi changes, copyright (c) 1986
     Technology Research Ltd (proprietary), the 5.04T changes "Copyright C.C. 1991" (from the ROM text).

   If you own the rights to one of them and want it removed, open an issue.

2. T80 (src/rtl/t80/) and tv80 (src/rtl/tv80/)
   -------------------------------------------
   T80: copyright (c) 2001-2002 Daniel Wallner, (c) 2018 Sorgelig and the other authors named in the files, under
   the BSD-style license in the header of each file. tv80: copyright (c) 2004 Guy Hutchison, under the MIT-style
   license in the header of each file; tv80_quad.v and the generated tv80q_core.v / tv80q_reg.v are derived from it
   and keep that license. The headers must be kept.

3. VG93 model and the Beta Disk glue (src/rtl/vg93/) - HRDY
   ---------------------------------------------------------
   The 1818VG93 (WD FD1793) model vg93_*.v / *.vh is by HRDY (Dmitry Demyanenko,
   https://github.com/demyanenko-d/FD1793_1818VG93), which publishes no license; its rights stay with the author.
   hrdy_fdc.v and fdd_glue.v are made after epm570/bdi_top.v and epm570/fdd_glue.v of that repository (the data
   separator after fapch_zek by ZEK, ZX-Evolution). The microcode ROM (vg93-microcode-rom.hex) was dumped from the
   die by deathsoft and decoded by dr.Titus. The files came here through karabas-go-core-tsconf
   (https://github.com/andykarpov/karabas-go-core-tsconf, MIT License, copyright (c) 2024 Andy Karpov); the MIT
   License there and below covers only the changes made in those repositories, not the model of HRDY.

4. AY sound generator (src/rtl/sound/ay_psg.v, src/rtl/sound/turbosound.v)
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   The logic of the AY-3-8910 generator follows ym2149 of MikeJ and Sorgelig (ym2149.sv of the MiSTer cores):
   copyright (c) MikeJ - Jan 2005, copyright (c) 2016-2019 Sorgelig, under their BSD-style license: redistribution
   and use in source and synthesized forms, with or without modification, are permitted provided that the copyright
   notice, the list of conditions and the disclaimer are retained in the source and reproduced in the documentation
   of the synthesized form; the names of the authors may not be used to endorse or promote products derived from it
   without prior written permission. THIS CODE IS PROVIDED BY THE COPYRIGHT HOLDERS AND CONTRIBUTORS "AS IS" AND ANY
   EXPRESS OR IMPLIED WARRANTIES ARE DISCLAIMED. The rest of these two files is under the MIT License below.

5. karabas-go-modules (modules/, a git submodule)
   ----------------------------------------------
   Andy Karpov and contributors: the terms of that repository.

